sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch02-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Among highly locomotive animals that unite for each birth, doubtful forms ranked as species by some and varieties by others are rarely found within the same country but are common in separated areas.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Doubtful forms of mobile animals are rare within a country but common between areas";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter II, “Variation under Nature”; section “Doubtful species”. Scope: highly mobile sexually reproducing animals such as birds and insects"
}
